{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/662151-can-werewolves-work-with-changelings","id":662151,"title":"Can Werewolves work with Changelings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-12T13:53:01-07:00","id":662151,"title":"Can Werewolves work with Changelings","content":"A friend of mine loaned me his Werewolf the Forsaken book and I was just wondering if it would be possible to have a Werewolf character work with other changeling characters. Do their have to be certain conditions like the Werewolf has to view these changelings as part of his pact? Can he have a tribe or does he have to be tribeless? Do the changelings and the werewolf have to make a pledge?<br /> <br /> Also would their be any balancing issues when it comes to having such a campaign?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;A dark shape crawls out from your closet. At first it looks like it has a large zipper for a mouth, however as it gets closer you soon realize that it isn't a zipper at all but rows of sharp yellow teeth!&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7343-werescythe","name":"Werescythe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T14:05:06-07:00","id":662186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werescythe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/662151-can-werewolves-work-with-changelings#post662151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A friend of mine loaned me his Werewolf the Forsaken book and I was just wondering if it would be possible to have a Werewolf character work with other changeling characters. Do their have to be certain conditions like the Werewolf has to view these changelings as part of his pact? Can he have a tribe or does he have to be tribeless? Do the changelings and the werewolf have to make a pledge?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they could be an 'honorary' member of the pack in first edition if you wanted, but you don't need to be part of a pack to work with a werewolf. In second edition they opened up the rules to allow other things to join packs, from animals to supernaturals. The Changeling wouldn't have a tribe, but the Werewolf could make a loyalty pledge with them.<br /> <br /> Obviously you could just toss the rules out the window and decide to let changelings be full fledged packmates.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also would their be any balancing issues when it comes to having such a campaign? </div> </div> </div>Changelings don't have an easy way into the Shadow, which tends to be one of the big things werewolves deal with, but if the werewolf eschewed the spirit-world they'd be fine. Werewolves don't have an easy way into the Hedge but I think doors can be opened for them by changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-12-2015, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T01:43:03-07:00","id":664049,"title":"","content":"Correct. Doors opened by Changelings can be used by anybody. Bringing a werewolf in the Hedge though is rather dangerous since it wreaks havoc on the internal balance of the werewolf.<br /> <br /> Personally I think that if you mix the two game lines you are making things hard on yourself if combats are an important part of the game. The things that challenge a werewolf probably destroy changelings. Than again, I have never been a particular big fan of mixing splat books, and not just because of mechanical balance issues. They also pose a problem story wise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T01:17:13-07:00","id":665456,"title":"","content":"The main idea I have for my campaign was to have Changelings and some Human Hunters kind of working together in this small club (of sorts) to protect a city from some supernatural threats (as well as keep each other safe from the True Fae). I was just wondering if it would be wise to include werewolves as a character choice option?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;A dark shape crawls out from your closet. At first it looks like it has a large zipper for a mouth, however as it gets closer you soon realize that it isn't a zipper at all but rows of sharp yellow teeth!&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7343-werescythe","name":"Werescythe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T17:05:41-07:00","id":666211,"title":"","content":"I am running a game with 3 Changelings, 2 Werewolves, and a Vampire and Sin-Eater. It works fine. As I am using 2e Werewolf the Werewolves have an overall power advantage, but Changelings bring some pretty potent tricks to the table. It works fine. The Vamp is the only hinky part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\